  "details": "This is a bit of a more intrusive request(?) compared to others that I have made in the past, but after dealing with poor experiences had by friends on now six different occasions - I get a lot of friends to play - changing one setting has consistently proven beneficial: Disabling MSAA. \n\nMany times when a new friend complains about frame issues, the first thing I ask after their safety settings is *\"have you disabled MSAA\"*. In all scenarios where they have not, typical frame-time improvements sit at around -9ms to -12ms depending on hardware. This is not a small amount by any stretch of the imagination, and I wish I were exaggerating these numbers, but I am not.\n\nThis is compounded with the fact that VR headsets through SteamVR can (and often do, by default) run at >100% resolution, meaning there is super-sampling already going on to partially mitigate aliasing to some extent. For this reason, MSAA is less useful than it would otherwise be, and I believe it would be better for it to be opt-in as a user choice to get additional quality on top of what they may have already, rather than a default which harms the user's performance.",
